 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Ibrahim gets no motif and no figure; no idol, star, moon or sun drawn, and 76-77 use the geometric mood (no sky). «هذا ربي» is glossed each time as argument with the opponent (As-Sa'di «على وجه التنزل مع الخصم», Al-Muyassar «على سبيل استدراج الخصم»), never as his belief. Geometric for «ملكوت السماوات والأرض». STAGING v4: c1: Ibrahim (blue drop) speaks to his father (one faceless man) in a town; the idols are never drawn (Ibrahim shakes his head at 74:7, points at his father at 74:10). 75: he looks up, a stars plate for the heavens. c2: at night with his people (3 men; Al-Muyassar: he debated his people, who worshipped the stars). The star and the moon are only the night sky of the stage (a sparkle on the sky at 76:6 and 77:3); their setting is a tilt of the camera to the ground (76:11, 77:9). Nothing is drawn, gestured or zoomed on 76:8-9 and 77:6-7: he speaks to his people (as argument, both tafsirs), never looks up, bows or raises hands there; no glow. No plate in c2."
 },
